          "text": "Direct answer: **the initial ones — carry the original baseline forward on model switch.** That reverses what I recommended last turn. I bundled the two triggers together because both have a cold cache, and that was the wrong axis to group them on.\n\n## Why the two triggers aren't the same thing\n\n**Compaction is a context boundary.** The model's view of the conversation is being rewritten anyway. Refreshing the chat list there is coherent — the context was rebuilt, here is the current picture.\n\n**A model switch is a provider boundary.** The conversation is unchanged; only who's reading it changed. Silently changing what the assistant knows about the user's other chats because they switched models is semantically incoherent, and you'd have to explain it to anyone who noticed.\n\nThere's also a mechanical asymmetry I missed, and it's the stronger argument:\n\n```\nCOMPACTION                                 MODEL SWITCH\nhistory before uptoSeq is REPLACED         history is UNTOUCHED\nby the checkpoint → most stale deltas      → every prior delta stays\ndisappear on their own                       verbatim in messages\n\nre-bake lands on a mostly-clean rail       re-bake orphans all of them\n```\n\nAt compaction, `buildContext` already drops everything at or below `uptoSeq` — the old deltas mostly evaporate with it. At a model switch nothing is dropped, so a fresh baseline strands every delta ever appended.\n\nThe free-refresh argument for switching is real but weak: it's an *opportunity*, not a requirement, and taking it costs you a mutable baseline plus a supersession marker at a moment when nothing about the conversation changed.\n\n## Revised\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Re-bake trigger** | **Compaction only** |\n| **Model switch** | Carry the original baseline forward; re-render it through the new template (new prompt text, new snapshot row, same chat list) |\n| **Supersession marker** | Needed at compaction only — for deltas after `uptoSeq` that survive absorption. Not needed at model switch, since nothing is superseded |\n\nOne trigger, one sentence: *the baseline is resolved at chat creation and re-resolved at each compaction.*\n\n## One correction to something I claimed\n\nI said re-baking at model switch \"dissolves the orphaning problem.\" It doesn't — I conflated two things. Orphaning is: **the new model's prompt file omits the digest block**, so the baseline is absent regardless of whether it's fresh or original, while deltas keep arriving. That needs its own fix either way: **when the active template renders no digest block, suppress digest deltas for that turn.** Mechanically, the prompt loader has to report whether the block rendered, and the delta renderer has to read that — a small, real coupling, and it's on the open list independent of everything above.\n\n## Open list\n\n1. **Unpin appends — in or out?** I recommend in.\n2. **Confirm the gating hierarchy and field names** (`historySharing` master default-on / `historyDigest` sub default-off), and the separate-axis call vs `personalization.enabled`.\n3. **Orphaning mechanism** — confirm \"block absent → deltas suppressed\" as the rule.\n\nThose three and I'll write the proposal.",
